cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Why Some LLMs Have a Hidden Reasoning Knob:
  Rare Full-Attention Bottlenecks in Hybrid Architectures
  and a 44-byte Quantization Recovery
message: >-
  If you use this software or patch in your research,
  please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Akito
    family-names: Hirai
    email: morphicode.jp@gmail.com
    orcid: ''
repository-code: 'https://github.com/morphicode_jp/f32-patch-gemma'
url: 'https://huggingface.co/morphicode_jp/gemma-4-31B-it-basin-b-Q2_K'
abstract: >-
  A training-free, calibration-free 44-byte F32 patch
  applied to 11 layer_output_scale weights of Gemma 4 31B
  yields +13.25pt HellaSwag accuracy improvement on the
  Q2_K quantization. The mechanism — rare full-attention
  bottleneck slack in hybrid LLMs — is validated across
  4 model families.
keywords:
  - LLM
  - quantization
  - gemma
  - hybrid-architecture
  - mechanistic-interpretability
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: '2026-05-20'
